        "knowledge_point_id": "79107609-77e6-55e9-970d-da63c39daf0a",
        "knowledge_point": "Finding the Cartesian Equation of a Curve Defined Parametrically",
        "problem": "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{t-5}{2},\\,\\,\\,y=({t}^{2}-25)(t-4),\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{t-5}{2}\\,⇒\\,t=2x+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=2x+5$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =((2x+5)^{2}-25)(2x+5-4) \\\\  & =(4{x}^{2}+20x+25-25)(2x+1) \\\\  & =(4{x}^{2}+20x)(2x+1) \\\\  & =4x(x+5)(2x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=4x(x+5)(2x+1).$",
