    {
      "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14097078",
      "id": "q-117666",
      "status": "supported",
      "reason": null,
      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-117666",
        "knowledge_point_id": "ec980fcb-97ed-5c60-94de-0521d9d7df27",
        "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Definite Integral of a Piecewise Continuous Function Given the Function Expression",
        "problem": "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{-5}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}7-3x, & x<-1 \\\\ 10, & x\\ge -1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-5}^{-1}(7-3x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}10\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(7x-3\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}){|}_{-5}^{-1}+10x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =[7(-1)-3\\frac{(-1)^{2}}{2}-7(-5)+3\\frac{(-5)^{2}}{2}]+10[(1)-(-1)] \\\\  & =[28+36]+10[2] \\\\  & =64+20 \\\\  & =84.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
